Bundled third-party code
------------------------

dist/ contains a prebundled copy of @classcad/smlibwasm 0.6.2
(https://github.com/awv-informatik/smlibpy, directory js):

  smlibwasm
  Copyright (c) 2026 AWV Informatik AG. Licensed under the MIT License
  (licenses/smlibwasm-LICENSE).

  dist/smlibwasm.wasm and the loader inside the bundle contain the SMLib solid modeling
  kernel and its SM_API wrapper from USD BRep, compiled with Emscripten, and code taken
  from USD BRep's Python bindings (SmPyLib):

    USD BRep
    Copyright (c) 2020-2026, NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (licenses/usd-brep-LICENSE).
    https://github.com/NVIDIA-Omniverse/usd-brep

  A few USD BRep source files are compiled from copies modified by AWV Informatik AG to
  fix defects; the copies, each with a notice of what was changed, are in
  third_party/patches of the smlibpy repository, whose third_party/patches/README.md
  lists the changes. dist/smlibwasm.wasm is the unmodified file from the npm package.

  The Emscripten runtime in the loader is used under the MIT License
  (licenses/emscripten-LICENSE).

  The static dictionary of the Brotli compression format (RFC 7932, appendix A) is
  included unmodified:

    Brotli
    Copyright (c) 2009, 2010, 2013-2016 by the Brotli Authors.
    https://github.com/google/brotli
    Licensed under the MIT License (same terms as LICENSE).

Not included: the upstream package's default text font (its dist/_fonts.js and the font's
licence file). The bundle replaces that module with an empty one, so Text() has no
default font and fails with an "unsupported" error. Everything shipped here is under the
MIT License or the Apache License 2.0.

The WebAssembly module's strings include "Open CASCADE Topology" version banners: they
belong to smlibwasm's reader and writer of the .brep file format (exportBrep/importBrep),
not to OCCT code; no OCCT library is part of this package.
